ctionable.\n\n    Wait, I need to make sure I don't sound like a UI designer.\n    \"布局\" usually means layout/design. In health, it means schedule/plan.\n    I will explicitly mention \"Plan/Schedule\".\n\n    Final Version:\n    您好，我是 Spark 健康助手。您是指**健康计划布局**（如饮食、运动日程）吗？\n\n    为了提供准确建议，请补充：\n    1. **目标**（减重、增肌、调理等）\n    2. **限制**（时间、设备、忌口）\n\n    收到后，我立刻为您生成可执行方案。\n\n    *Wait, is \"把布局出\" actually \"把步数出\" (output steps)?* No.\n    *Is it \"把病历出\" (medical record)?* No.\n    *Most likely:* They want a plan.\n    *Okay, ready to output.*\n\n    One more thing: The instruction says \"优先提供准确、简洁、可执行的健康建议\".\n    If I just ask questions, am I violating \"Provide advice\"?\n    Technically, clarifying intent is necessary to provide *accurate* advice.\n    But maybe I can give a generic tip while asking?\n    No, generic tips might be useless.\n    Better to ask clearly.\n\n    Wait, I can interpret \"布局\" as \"Layout of a healthy day\".\n    I can provide a *template* immediately.\n    \"如果您需要一日健康流程，通常包含：早餐高蛋白、午间均衡膳食、晚间适度运动及 7-8 小时睡眠。\"\n    Then ask for specifics.\n    This satisfies \"provide advice\".\n\n    Revised Plan:\n    1. Acknowledge.\n    2. Give a generic \"Healthy Layout\" template (Actionable advice).\n    3. Ask for specifics to customize.\n\n    Draft:\n    您好，我是 Spark 健康助手。关于“健康布局”，这里有一份通用的一日健康流程供您参考：\n\n    1. **早晨**：起床后温水一杯 + 10 分钟拉伸。\n    2. **午餐**：主食粗细搭配 + 优质蛋白 + 大量蔬菜。\n    3. **下午**：每坐 1 小时起身活动 5 分钟。\n    4. **晚上**：睡前 1 小时远离屏幕，保证 7 小时睡眠。\n\n    如需个性化定制（如减脂、增肌），请告诉我您的目标和身体状况。\n\n    This is much better! It provides actionable advice immediately while staying open for customization. It fits \"Accurate, Concise, Actionable\".\n\n    Let's refine the generic advice to be very standard and safe.\n    Morning water, stretching. Balanced lunch. Breaks. Sleep.\n    Sounds good.\n\n    Final check: \"这是小明星\" - Should I address them as Little Star?\n    The system instruction says \"Use user language\". It doesn't explicitly say use their name if known. But \"这是小明星\" might be the user telling me their name is \"Little Star\".\n    If I say \"Hello Little Star\", it adds personalization.\n    But since it's ambiguous if it's the user's name or just text, I'll stick to neutral \"您好\". Or I can assume it's the name since it's at the start of the context.\n    Actually, looking at the prompt structure:\n    `系统`: `这是小明星` (This is Little Star)\n    `系统`: `你是 Spark...`\n    This looks like the *System* is telling *Me* (the model) that the user is named Little Star.\n    So I should address them as \"小明星\".\n    Wait, reading carefully:\n    `这是小明星` (Line 1)\n    `你是 Spark 健康助手...` (Line 2)\n    Usually, these lines define the persona. \"This is Little Star\" might be the *name of the persona*? No, \"You are Spark Health Assistant\".\n    Maybe \"This is Little Star\" is the *User's Name*.\n    Okay, I will try to incorporate it gently or stick to neutral. Safest is neutral unless sure.\n    Actually, often prompts start with context like \"This is [Context]\".\n    I will play it safe and just be polite.\n\n    Wait, re-reading the prompt block provided in the task description:\n    `这是小明星`\n    `你是 Spark 健康助手...`\n    `用户`\n    `把布局出`\n\n    It seems \"这是小明星\" is part of the system context. It might mean \"The user is Little Star\".\n    I will address them politely. If I call them \"小明星\", it shows I read the context.\n    But the instruction says \"Use user language\".\n    Okay, I'll skip the name to avoid assumption error, focus on the task.\n\n    Wait, one more thought: \"把布局出\" -> \"把\" (Ba) \"布\" (Bu) \"局\" (Ju) \"出\" (Chu).\n    Could it be \"把不举出\" (Erectile dysfunction)? No.\n    Could it be \"把补剂出\" (Supplements)?\n    Given the ambiguity, the \"Generic Plan Template\" approach is best. It covers the most bases of \"layout\".\n\n    Finalizing the content:\n    1. Greeting + Role.\n    2. Generic Healthy Day Layout (Actionable).\n    3. Call to action for customization.\n\n    Let's write it.\n    \"您好，我是 Sp